WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:08.200
ANNOUNCER: Setting a new
world record of 2:22:43,

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.867
Joan Benoit moves women's
marathoning to the next level.

00:00:12.867 --> 00:00:14.950
JOAN BENOIT SAMUELSON: Can
anybody run at any age?

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.350
Yes, and that's why
I'm still running well

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.325
into my sixth decade.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:24.880
This class is for
runners, aspiring runners,

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.390
and for people who just have a
general interest in our sport.

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:30.670
I'm going to talk
about technique,

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:34.060
stretching and strengthening
exercises, and the importance

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.100
of setting goals.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:39.920
Running should be something that
you look forward to every day

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.490
however many times you're
getting out there to run.

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:45.700
The most important things are
finding the proper footwear,

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:48.610
making it fun,
making it purposeful,

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.370
and making it something
that fits your lifestyle.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:54.850
One tip for new
runners is to think

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:57.940
about your running in minutes
as opposed to distance.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:01.090
And whether it's 15 minutes
a day or every other day,

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:03.940
the fact of the matter
is that you're doing it.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:06.880
There weren't many sports
available to young girls when

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.580
I was growing up because
Title IX legislation hadn't

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:11.560
been enacted into law.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:15.880
Eventually it passed
in 1972, and that's

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:19.390
when I discovered that I had
a real passion for running.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:24.760
And I often asked myself
if Title IX hadn't passed,

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:27.400
what would I be doing today?

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:31.420
It's up to you to discover
how far the journey of running

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:32.530
is going to take you.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:35.350
And if you follow the
lessons in my class,

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:37.540
you will have running
as part of your life

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:39.550
for a long, long time.

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:44.100
I'm Joan Benoit Samuelson,
and this is MasterClass.

